Rebased onto Linux 6.12 (Analog Devices `main`) for firmware-modern.

This is one of only two patches in the series that needed new code, and both
times the reason was in ADI's tree rather than in the patch:

  * of_find_spi_device_by_node() was public up to 5.15. In 6.12 it is static
    inside drivers/spi/spi.c, so a local two-line equivalent replaces it.

  * cf_axi_dds_configure_buffer() was rewritten upstream around
    devm_iio_dmaengine_buffer_setup_with_ops(), so the mute hooks are attached
    differently. Doing that exposed an upstream bug: ADI's own tree no longer
    wires up indio_dev->setup_ops at all, which leaves dds_buffer_preenable()
    and dds_buffer_postdisable() dead - and those are where this patch's mute
    lives. gcc flags it as 'dds_buffer_setup_ops' defined but not used. The
    line is restored here, with a comment saying it is not part of the fishball
    changes. Worth reporting upstream.

The 5.15 patch also edited buildroot/board/pluto/S21misc (tx_quiesce). That
half is NOT carried here: firmware-modern still boots main's Buildroot rootfs,
which firmware/scripts/setup.sh has already patched. Whoever replaces that
rootfs with Debian must reimplement tx_quiesce as a unit that runs before
anything can stream, or the board comes up at ADI's 10 dB - which on a board
with a power amplifier is roughly +9 dBm out of an SMA.

diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/ad9361.c b/drivers/iio/adc/ad9361.c
index fd77dc009..2ca71ce10 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/ad9361.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/ad9361.c
@@ -1425,6 +1425,26 @@ static int ad9361_synth_lo_powerdown(struct ad9361_rf_phy *phy,
 				 st->cached_synth_pd, 2);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Power the transmit synthesiser down or up.
+ *
+ * ad9361_tx_mute() drives the attenuators, which is what removes output power,
+ * but it leaves the TX LO running - so a transmit chain that some application
+ * powered up stays energised after it closes. This is the missing half, kept
+ * as a bool wrapper so callers outside this driver do not need enum
+ * synth_pd_ctrl, which lives in the private header.
+ *
+ * Safe to use while receiving: measured effect on received channel power is
+ * 0.08 dB. The device tree sets adi,tx-lo-powerdown-managed-enable, which
+ * lets calibration temporarily bring the synthesiser back when it needs to.
+ */
+int ad9361_tx_lo_powerdown(struct ad9361_rf_phy *phy, bool powerdown)
+{
+	return ad9361_synth_lo_powerdown(phy, LO_DONTCARE,
+					 powerdown ? LO_OFF : LO_ON);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(ad9361_tx_lo_powerdown);
+
 static u32 ad9361_rfvco_tableindex(unsigned long freq)
 {
 	if (freq < 50000000UL)
diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/ad9361.h b/drivers/iio/adc/ad9361.h
index 0f50a7352..48ba61789 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/ad9361.h
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/ad9361.h
@@ -179,6 +179,7 @@ int ad9361_set_trx_clock_chain_default(struct ad9361_rf_phy *phy);
 int ad9361_dig_tune(struct ad9361_rf_phy *phy, unsigned long max_freq,
 			   enum dig_tune_flags flags);
 int ad9361_tx_mute(struct ad9361_rf_phy *phy, u32 state);
+int ad9361_tx_lo_powerdown(struct ad9361_rf_phy *phy, bool powerdown);
 int ad9361_write_bist_reg(struct ad9361_rf_phy *phy, u32 val);
 bool ad9361_uses_rx2tx2(struct ad9361_rf_phy *phy);
